Two thoughts responding to two different people...

>Not really. Once you have one, you can create as many as you want. Now,
>image what would happen if people could kill anything in one attack.

Even if there's a chance of splattering yourself and killing yourself
as well as the target?  That's why there's provision for splatter when
throwing or hitting with it -- not only is that realistic (anyone who's
ever shattered a bottle IRL knows that the stuff inside goes absolutely
everywhere) but it also makes it a more risky weapon.

As to Gnomes armed with ! o green slime being a cause of early
instadeath -- not if you have some source of fire, like a potion of oil
or some such.   The player gets at least three turns on the slime
counter in the worst case -- enough time to get a fire-making source
and burn it off.

Of course,  a weak character might die from the burning outright, or at
least be weakened enough that other monsters would have a better chance
of killing him.  But if you wanted a safe life, you shouldn't be in the
dungeon :).  

